IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc16-dna-definitions.l4 -- section 487.04 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: Forensic DNA Analysis, Definitions.
-- Part agent ccc16. Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Imports the keel's core only.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- The French equivalents in parentheses after a defined term are quoted with the line, not encoded.
--
-- How the lists are tested (the convention PLAN.md R1 asks parts to share): an offence is a core `Provision of the Code`: `section` is the
-- section number as a decimal (151; 83.18; 320.16) and `subsection` is "" or what follows the section number in the Code's own words:
-- "(4.1)" for subsection 7(4.1); "(a)" for paragraph 245(a); "(1)(d)" for paragraph 348(1)(d); "(1)(b)(i)" for subparagraph 465(1)(b)(i).
-- A list row with `the subsection` "" names a whole section, so it matches that section with any subsection; a row with a subsection
-- matches that section and exactly that subsection.
-- Which instrument the provision belongs to (this Act, the 1970 Criminal Code at one of three vintages, the Cannabis Act ...) is a second
-- fact of the offence (`where that provision is found`), because paragraphs (b), (c), (c.01), (c.02), (c.03) and (c.1) name other texts.
--
-- How a result reads (see NOTES.md, Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING): `JUST TRUE` the text covers the case in its own words;
-- `JUST FALSE` the text says no ("means ... namely", "other than", "other than for the purposes of subsection 487.05(1)");
-- `NOTHING` not covered (a meaning left to another Act, or a maximum punishment the offence's own section does not state).

§ `Section 487.04 -- the scope of the definitions`

-- 487.04 In this section and in sections 487.05 to 487.0911, ... (the definitions that follow)
-- Section numbers are decimals, so "sections 487.05 to 487.0911" is a range test (487.051 and 487.0911 are inside; 487.1 is not).
-- src:9292 | 487.04 In this section and in sections 487.05 to 487.0911,
@ref s 487.04 (the scope: this section and sections 487.05 to 487.0911) (src:9292)
GIVEN `the section the term is used in` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.04 the definitions apply in the section` MEANS
    IF    `the section the term is used in` EQUALS 487.04
       OR (`the section the term is used in` AT LEAST 487.05 AND `the section the term is used in` AT MOST 487.0911)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In this section and in sections 487.05 to 487.0911,"

§ `Section 487.04 -- the plain definitions: adult, DNA, young person, provincial court judge, Young Offenders Act`

-- "adult" has the meaning assigned by subsection 2(1) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act: that Act is not among the sources, so the answer is an input.
-- src:9293 | adult has the meaning assigned by subsection 2(1) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act; (adulte)
@ref s 487.04 "adult" (src:9293)
GIVEN `the person is an adult within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.04 adult` MEANS
    `the person is an adult within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act`   -- passes JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING through; NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) when the Youth Criminal Justice Act answer is not given

-- src:9295 | DNA means deoxyribonucleic acid; (ADN)
@ref s 487.04 "DNA" (src:9295)
GIVEN `the substance is deoxyribonucleic acid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.04 DNA` MEANS
    IF `the substance is deoxyribonucleic acid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "DNA means deoxyribonucleic acid"

-- "young person" has the meaning assigned by subsection 2(1) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act or subsection 2(1) of the Young Offenders Act, as the case may be.
DECLARE `s 487.04 which Act assigns the meaning of young person` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.04 the Youth Criminal Justice Act`
    `s 487.04 the Young Offenders Act`
    `s 487.04 the text does not say which of the two Acts applies`

-- src:9543 | young person has the meaning assigned by subsection 2(1) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act or subsection 2(1) of the Young Offenders Act, as the case may be. (adolescent)
@ref s 487.04 "young person" (src:9543)
GIVEN `which Act assigns the meaning` IS A `s 487.04 which Act assigns the meaning of young person`
      `the person is a young person within subsection 2(1) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a young person within subsection 2(1) of the Young Offenders Act` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.04 young person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which Act assigns the meaning`
    WHEN `s 487.04 the Youth Criminal Justice Act` THEN `the person is a young person within subsection 2(1) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act`
    WHEN `s 487.04 the Young Offenders Act` THEN `the person is a young person within subsection 2(1) of the Young Offenders Act`
    WHEN `s 487.04 the text does not say which of the two Acts applies` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "as the case may be" does not say which Act applies

-- "provincial court judge", in relation to a young person, includes a youth justice court judge within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act.
-- src:9424 | provincial court judge, in relation to a young person, includes a youth justice court judge within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act; (juge de la cour provinciale)
@ref s 487.04 "provincial court judge" (src:9424)
GIVEN `the person is a young person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the judge is a youth justice court judge within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.04 provincial court judge, in relation to a young person, includes a youth justice court judge` MEANS
    IF (`the person is a young person` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the judge is a youth justice court judge within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes a youth justice court judge" lists a case the term takes in and does not say what else it is

-- src:9542 | Young Offenders Act means chapter Y-1 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1985; (Loi sur les jeunes contrevenants)
@ref s 487.04 "Young Offenders Act" (src:9542)
GIVEN `the instrument is chapter Y-1 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1985` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.04 Young Offenders Act` MEANS
    IF `the instrument is chapter Y-1 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1985`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Young Offenders Act means chapter Y-1 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1985"

§ `Section 487.04 -- forensic DNA analysis`

-- The five kinds of bodily substance the two paragraphs name, and the extent of analysis each paragraph gives.
DECLARE `s 487.04 how the bodily substance came to be analysed` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.04 taken from a person in execution of a warrant under section 487.05`
    `s 487.04 provided voluntarily in the course of an investigation of a designated offence`
    `s 487.04 taken from a person under an order made under section 487.051`
    `s 487.04 taken from a person under an authorization granted under section 487.055 or 487.091`
    `s 487.04 a bodily substance referred to in paragraph 487.05(1)(b)`
    `s 487.04 a bodily substance that came to be analysed in some other way`

DECLARE `s 487.04 the extent of the forensic DNA analysis` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.04 analysis of the substance, comparison of the results with the results of the analysis of the DNA in the substance referred to in paragraph 487.05(1)(b), and any incidental tests associated with that analysis`   -- (a)
    `s 487.04 analysis of the bodily substance`   -- (b)

-- src:9296 | forensic DNA analysis
-- src:9297 | (a) in relation to a bodily substance that is taken from a person in execution of a warrant under section 487.05, means forensic DNA analysis of the bodily substance and the comparison of the results of that analysis with the results of the analysis of the DNA in the bodily substance referred to in paragraph 487.05(1)(b), and includes any incidental tests associated with that analysis, and
-- src:9298 | (b) in relation to a bodily substance that is provided voluntarily in the course of an investigation of a designated offence or is taken from a person under an order made under section 487.051 or an authorization granted under section 487.055 or 487.091, or to a bodily substance referred to in paragraph 487.05(1)(b), means forensic DNA analysis of the bodily substance; (analyse génétique)
@ref s 487.04 "forensic DNA analysis" (a), (b) (src:9296-9298)
GIVEN how IS A `s 487.04 how the bodily substance came to be analysed`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 487.04 the extent of the forensic DNA analysis`
`s 487.04 forensic DNA analysis` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `s 487.04 taken from a person in execution of a warrant under section 487.05` THEN
        JUST `s 487.04 analysis of the substance, comparison of the results with the results of the analysis of the DNA in the substance referred to in paragraph 487.05(1)(b), and any incidental tests associated with that analysis`
    WHEN `s 487.04 provided voluntarily in the course of an investigation of a designated offence` THEN JUST `s 487.04 analysis of the bodily substance`
    WHEN `s 487.04 taken from a person under an order made under section 487.051` THEN JUST `s 487.04 analysis of the bodily substance`
    WHEN `s 487.04 taken from a person under an authorization granted under section 487.055 or 487.091` THEN JUST `s 487.04 analysis of the bodily substance`
    WHEN `s 487.04 a bodily substance referred to in paragraph 487.05(1)(b)` THEN JUST `s 487.04 analysis of the bodily substance`
    WHEN `s 487.04 a bodily substance that came to be analysed in some other way` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraphs (a) and (b) speak "in relation to" the five kinds of bodily substance they name

§ `Section 487.04 -- primary designated offence: the lists, as the text writes them`

-- The offence provisions the text names, one row each. A row with "" for the subsection names the whole section.
DECLARE `s 487.04 listed provision` HAS
    `the section`      IS A NUMBER
    `the subsection`   IS A STRING

-- Where the provision is found: the Code as it now reads, the same Code at the vintages some paragraphs name, or another instrument.
DECLARE `s 487.04 where the provision is found` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.04 this Act as it reads now`
    `s 487.04 this Act as it read from time to time before the day on which the paragraph that names it comes into force`   -- primary (c.02), (c.03)
    `s 487.04 this Act as it read from time to time before July 1, 1990`   -- secondary (d)
    `s 487.04 this Act as it read from time to time before the day on which section 14 of the Act to amend the Criminal Code (offences relating to conveyances) comes into force`   -- secondary (d.1), (d.2)
    `s 487.04 the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read from time to time before January 4, 1983`   -- primary (b)
    `s 487.04 the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read from time to time before January 1, 1988`   -- primary (c)
    `s 487.04 the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as enacted by section 19 of chapter 125 of the Statutes of Canada, 1980-81-82-83`   -- primary (c.01)
    `s 487.04 the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act`   -- primary (c.1)
    `s 487.04 the Cannabis Act`   -- secondary (a.1)
    `s 487.04 the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act`   -- secondary (b)
    `s 487.04 another instrument`

DECLARE `s 487.04 how the person is charged` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.04 with the listed offence itself`
    `s 487.04 with an attempt to commit the listed offence`
    `s 487.04 with a conspiracy to commit the listed offence`

-- The purposes the text distinguishes: subsection 487.05(1) (the warrant) and section 487.051 (the order on conviction).
DECLARE `s 487.04 the purpose the answer is wanted for` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.04 the purposes of subsection 487.05(1)`
    `s 487.04 the purposes of section 487.051`
    `s 487.04 another purpose`

DECLARE `s 487.04 facts of the offence` HAS
    `the provision that creates the offence` IS A `Provision of the Code`
    `where that provision is found` IS A `s 487.04 where the provision is found`
    `how the person is charged` IS A `s 487.04 how the person is charged`
    `the purpose` IS A `s 487.04 the purpose the answer is wanted for`
    `the offence may be prosecuted by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence is prosecuted by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the maximum imprisonment for the offence` IS AN Imprisonment
    `the intent of an assault under subsection 246(1) is to commit an offence referred to in subparagraphs (b)(i) to (vi)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- One row of a list names a provision; the offence is on the list if some row names it.
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the list` IS A LIST OF `s 487.04 listed provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 487.04 the provision is on the list` MEANS
    any (GIVEN row YIELD (row's `the section` EQUALS `the provision`'s `section`) AND (row's `the subsection` EQUALS "" OR row's `the subsection` EQUALS `the provision`'s `subsection`)) `the list`

