§ `Section 487.04 -- primary designated offence: the definition`

-- Paragraphs (a) to (c.03): the offence is on the list that belongs to the instrument and vintage it is found in.
-- (b)(vii): subsection 246(1) is a primary designated offence only "if the intent is to commit an offence referred to in subparagraphs (i) to (vi)".
-- src:9299 | primary designated offence means
-- src:9300 | (a) an offence under any of the following provisions, namely,
-- src:9342 | (a.1) an offence under any of the following provisions, namely,
-- src:9389 | (b) an offence under any of the following provisions of the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as they read from time to time before January 4, 1983, namely,
-- src:9397 | (vii) subsection 246(1) (assault with intent) if the intent is to commit an offence referred to in subparagraphs (i) to (vi),
-- src:9398 | (c) an offence under any of the following provisions of the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as they read from time to time before January 1, 1988:
-- src:9405 | (c.01) an offence under any of the following provisions of the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as enacted by section 19 of An Act to amend the Criminal Code in relation to sexual offences and other offences against the person and to amend certain other Acts in relation thereto or in consequence thereof, chapter 125 of the Statutes of Canada, 1980-81-82-83:
-- src:9409 | (c.02) an offence under any of the following provisions of this Act, as they read from time to time before the day on which this paragraph comes into force:
-- src:9414 | (c.03) an offence under any of paragraphs 212(1)(a) to (h) (procuring) of this Act, as they read from time to time before the day on which this paragraph comes into force,
@ref s 487.04 "primary designated offence" (a) to (c.03) (src:9299-9414)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 487.04 facts of the offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 487.04 primary designated offence paragraphs (a) to (c.03) list the provision` MEANS
        (    facts's `where that provision is found` EQUALS `s 487.04 this Act as it reads now`
         AND (`on list` `s 487.04 primary designated offence (a) provisions` OR `on list` `s 487.04 primary designated offence (a.1) provisions`))
     OR (    facts's `where that provision is found` EQUALS `s 487.04 the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read from time to time before January 4, 1983`
         AND `on list` `s 487.04 primary designated offence (b) provisions`
         AND ((NOT `is subsection 246(1)`) OR facts's `the intent of an assault under subsection 246(1) is to commit an offence referred to in subparagraphs (b)(i) to (vi)`))
     OR (    facts's `where that provision is found` EQUALS `s 487.04 the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read from time to time before January 1, 1988`
         AND `on list` `s 487.04 primary designated offence (c) provisions`)
     OR (    facts's `where that provision is found` EQUALS `s 487.04 the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as enacted by section 19 of chapter 125 of the Statutes of Canada, 1980-81-82-83`
         AND `on list` `s 487.04 primary designated offence (c.01) provisions`)
     OR (    facts's `where that provision is found` EQUALS `s 487.04 this Act as it read from time to time before the day on which the paragraph that names it comes into force`
         AND (`on list` `s 487.04 primary designated offence (c.02) provisions` OR `on list` `s 487.04 primary designated offence (c.03) provisions`))
    WHERE
        `on list` list MEANS `s 487.04 the provision is on the list` (facts's `the provision that creates the offence`) list
        `is subsection 246(1)` MEANS facts's `the provision that creates the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 246 AND facts's `the provision that creates the offence`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)"

-- src:9299 | primary designated offence means
-- src:9415 | (c.1) an offence under any of the following provisions of the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act, namely,
@ref s 487.04 "primary designated offence" (c.1) (src:9299-9415)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 487.04 facts of the offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 487.04 primary designated offence paragraph (c.1) lists the provision` MEANS
        facts's `where that provision is found` EQUALS `s 487.04 the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act`
    AND `s 487.04 the provision is on the list` (facts's `the provision that creates the offence`) `s 487.04 primary designated offence (c.1) provisions`

-- (d) an attempt to commit or, other than for the purposes of subsection 487.05(1), a conspiracy to commit an offence referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (c.03).
-- Paragraph (c.1) is not in that range, so an attempt or a conspiracy to commit a Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act offence is not within (d) (NOTES.md, finding).
-- src:9299 | primary designated offence means
-- src:9423 | (d) an attempt to commit or, other than for the purposes of subsection 487.05(1), a conspiracy to commit an offence referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (c.03); (infraction primaire)
@ref s 487.04 "primary designated offence" (d), and the definition as a whole (src:9299-9423)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 487.04 facts of the offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.04 the offence is a primary designated offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `how the person is charged`
    WHEN `s 487.04 with the listed offence itself` THEN
        IF `s 487.04 primary designated offence paragraphs (a) to (c.03) list the provision` facts OR `s 487.04 primary designated offence paragraph (c.1) lists the provision` facts
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "primary designated offence means" (the offence is not on any of the lists in paragraphs (a) to (c.1))
    WHEN `s 487.04 with an attempt to commit the listed offence` THEN
        IF `s 487.04 primary designated offence paragraphs (a) to (c.03) list the provision` facts
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an offence referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (c.03)" (the attempted offence is not in paragraphs (a) to (c.03))
    WHEN `s 487.04 with a conspiracy to commit the listed offence` THEN
        IF facts's `the purpose` EQUALS `s 487.04 the purposes of subsection 487.05(1)`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than for the purposes of subsection 487.05(1), a conspiracy to commit an offence"
        ELSE IF `s 487.04 primary designated offence paragraphs (a) to (c.03) list the provision` facts
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an offence referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (c.03)" (the offence conspired is not in paragraphs (a) to (c.03))

