§ `Section 487.04 -- secondary designated offence: the definition`

-- "for which the maximum punishment is imprisonment for five years or more": a term of five years or more, or life.
-- The Code's "Length of time" keeps years, months, days and a "less a day" flag: five years less a day is below five years.
GIVEN t IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 487.04 the term is five years or more` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (t's years TIMES 12 PLUS t's months) GREATER THAN 60 THEN TRUE
        IF (t's years TIMES 12 PLUS t's months) EQUALS 60 THEN ((t's days GREATER THAN 0) OR (NOT t's `less a day`))
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:9426 | (a) an offence under this Act that may be prosecuted by indictment — or, for section 487.051 to apply, is prosecuted by indictment — for which the maximum punishment is imprisonment for five years or more,
@ref s 487.04 "secondary designated offence" (a) (the maximum punishment) (src:9426)
GIVEN `the maximum imprisonment` IS AN Imprisonment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.04 the maximum punishment is imprisonment for five years or more` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the maximum imprisonment`
    WHEN `imprisonment for life` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` t THEN JUST (`s 487.04 the term is five years or more` t)
    WHEN `no imprisonment is stated` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the offence's own limb states no maximum imprisonment, so the maximum is for the provision that fixes it

-- "that may be prosecuted by indictment -- or, for section 487.051 to apply, is prosecuted by indictment": the second form applies when the answer is wanted for section 487.051.
-- src:9426 | (a) an offence under this Act that may be prosecuted by indictment — or, for section 487.051 to apply, is prosecuted by indictment — for which the maximum punishment is imprisonment for five years or more,
@ref s 487.04 "secondary designated offence" (a) (the mode of prosecution) (src:9426)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 487.04 facts of the offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 487.04 the offence may be prosecuted by indictment or, for section 487.051 to apply, is prosecuted by indictment` MEANS
    IF facts's `the purpose` EQUALS `s 487.04 the purposes of section 487.051`
    THEN facts's `the offence is prosecuted by indictment`
    ELSE facts's `the offence may be prosecuted by indictment`

-- (a), (a.1) and (b): an offence of this Act, the Cannabis Act (sections 9 to 14) or the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act (sections 5 to 7) that may be prosecuted by indictment, with a maximum of five years or more.
-- (c), (d), (d.1), (d.2): listed provisions of this Act (as it reads now, or at the vintage named); (d.2) with the same prosecution condition.
-- src:9426 | (a) an offence under this Act that may be prosecuted by indictment — or, for section 487.051 to apply, is prosecuted by indictment — for which the maximum punishment is imprisonment for five years or more,
-- src:9427 | (a.1) an offence under any of the following provisions of the Cannabis Act that may be prosecuted by indictment — or, for section 487.051 to apply, is prosecuted by indictment — for which the maximum punishment is imprisonment for five years or more:
-- src:9434 | (b) an offence under any of the following provisions of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act that may be prosecuted by indictment — or, for section 487.051 to apply, is prosecuted by indictment — for which the maximum punishment is imprisonment for five years or more:
-- src:9438 | (c) an offence under any of the following provisions of this Act:
-- src:9534 | (d) an offence under any of the following provisions of the Criminal Code, as they read from time to time before July 1, 1990:
-- src:9537 | (d.1) an offence under section 252, as it read from time to time before the day on which section 14 of An Act to amend the Criminal Code (offences relating to conveyances) and to make consequential amendments to other Acts comes into force,
-- src:9538 | (d.2) an offence under any of sections 249, 249.1, 249.2, 249.3, 249.4, 253, 254 and 255, as they read from time to time before the day on which section 14 of An Act to amend the Criminal Code (offences relating to conveyances) and to make consequential amendments to other Acts comes into force, that may be prosecuted by indictment or, for section 487.051 to apply, is prosecuted by indictment, and
@ref s 487.04 "secondary designated offence" (a), (a.1), (b), (c), (d), (d.1), (d.2) (src:9426-9538)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 487.04 facts of the offence`
      `paragraph (a.1) is to be counted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.04 secondary designated offence the answer of each of paragraphs (a) to (d.2)` MEANS
    LIST `paragraph (a)`, `the answer of paragraph (a.1)`, `paragraph (b)`, `paragraph (c)`, `paragraph (d)`, `paragraph (d.1)`, `paragraph (d.2)`
    WHERE
        `the answer of paragraph (a.1)` MEANS
            IF `paragraph (a.1) is to be counted`
            THEN `paragraph (a.1)`
            ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(i) an offence referred to in paragraph (a) or (b)" (paragraph (e)(i) names (a) and (b) and not (a.1))
        `where found` MEANS facts's `where that provision is found`
        `on list` list MEANS `s 487.04 the provision is on the list` (facts's `the provision that creates the offence`) list
        `the indictment condition and the five years` MEANS
            IF `s 487.04 the offence may be prosecuted by indictment or, for section 487.051 to apply, is prosecuted by indictment` facts
            THEN `s 487.04 the maximum punishment is imprisonment for five years or more` (facts's `the maximum imprisonment for the offence`)
            ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that may be prosecuted by indictment"
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS
            IF `where found` EQUALS `s 487.04 this Act as it reads now`
            THEN `the indictment condition and the five years`
            ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) an offence under this Act" (the provision is not of this Act as it reads now)
        `paragraph (a.1)` MEANS
            IF `where found` EQUALS `s 487.04 the Cannabis Act` AND `on list` `s 487.04 secondary designated offence (a.1) provisions`
            THEN `the indictment condition and the five years`
            ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a.1) an offence under any of the following provisions of the Cannabis Act"
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
            IF `where found` EQUALS `s 487.04 the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act` AND `on list` `s 487.04 secondary designated offence (b) provisions`
            THEN `the indictment condition and the five years`
            ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) an offence under any of the following provisions of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act"
        `paragraph (c)` MEANS
            IF `where found` EQUALS `s 487.04 this Act as it reads now` AND `on list` `s 487.04 secondary designated offence (c) provisions`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) an offence under any of the following provisions of this Act"
        `paragraph (d)` MEANS
            IF `where found` EQUALS `s 487.04 this Act as it read from time to time before July 1, 1990` AND `on list` `s 487.04 secondary designated offence (d) provisions`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) an offence under any of the following provisions of the Criminal Code, as they read from time to time before July 1, 1990"
        `paragraph (d.1)` MEANS
            IF `where found` EQUALS `s 487.04 this Act as it read from time to time before the day on which section 14 of the Act to amend the Criminal Code (offences relating to conveyances) comes into force` AND `on list` `s 487.04 secondary designated offence (d.1) provisions`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d.1) an offence under section 252, as it read from time to time before the day on which section 14"
        `paragraph (d.2)` MEANS
            IF `where found` EQUALS `s 487.04 this Act as it read from time to time before the day on which section 14 of the Act to amend the Criminal Code (offences relating to conveyances) comes into force` AND `on list` `s 487.04 secondary designated offence (d.2) provisions`
            THEN `the (d.2) prosecution condition`
            ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d.2) an offence under any of sections 249, 249.1, 249.2, 249.3, 249.4, 253, 254 and 255"
        `the (d.2) prosecution condition` MEANS
            IF `s 487.04 the offence may be prosecuted by indictment or, for section 487.051 to apply, is prosecuted by indictment` facts
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that may be prosecuted by indictment"

-- paragraph (a.1) is counted when the offence itself is asked about; it is not counted for an attempt or a conspiracy, because (e)(i) names (a) or (b) only.
-- One of the paragraphs' answers decides: any JUST TRUE gives JUST TRUE; otherwise any NOTHING gives NOTHING; otherwise JUST FALSE.
GIVEN answers IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.04 the paragraphs of a definition are read together` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF any (GIVEN a YIELD a EQUALS JUST TRUE) answers THEN JUST TRUE
        IF any (GIVEN a YIELD a EQUALS NOTHING) answers THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a paragraph turns on a maximum punishment the offence's own section does not state
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "secondary designated offence means an offence, other than a primary designated offence, that is" (no paragraph covers the offence)

-- (e) an attempt or a conspiracy (not, for the purposes of subsection 487.05(1), a conspiracy) to commit (i) an offence in paragraph (a) or (b), which, for section 487.051 to apply, is prosecuted by indictment, or (ii) an offence in any of paragraphs (c) to (d.2).
-- Paragraph (e)(i) names (a) and (b): it does not name (a.1), the Cannabis Act paragraph (NOTES.md, finding).
-- src:9539 | (e) an attempt to commit or, other than for the purposes of subsection 487.05(1), a conspiracy to commit
-- src:9540 | (i) an offence referred to in paragraph (a) or (b) — which, for section 487.051 to apply, is prosecuted by indictment, or
-- src:9541 | (ii) an offence referred to in any of paragraphs (c) to (d.2); (infraction secondaire)
@ref s 487.04 "secondary designated offence" (e)(i), (ii) (src:9539-9541)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 487.04 facts of the offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.04 secondary designated offence (e) an attempt or a conspiracy` MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `how the person is charged`
    WHEN `s 487.04 with the listed offence itself` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(e) an attempt to commit or, other than for the purposes of subsection 487.05(1), a conspiracy to commit" (the person is not charged with an attempt or a conspiracy)
    WHEN `s 487.04 with an attempt to commit the listed offence` THEN `the object offence`
    WHEN `s 487.04 with a conspiracy to commit the listed offence` THEN
        IF facts's `the purpose` EQUALS `s 487.04 the purposes of subsection 487.05(1)`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than for the purposes of subsection 487.05(1), a conspiracy to commit"
        ELSE `the object offence`
    WHERE
        `the answers` MEANS `s 487.04 secondary designated offence the answer of each of paragraphs (a) to (d.2)` facts FALSE
        `the object offence` MEANS
            `s 487.04 the paragraphs of a definition are read together` `the answers`   -- (a) and (b) as (e)(i) names them, (c) to (d.2) as (e)(ii) names them: (a.1) is named in neither

-- src:9425 | secondary designated offence means an offence, other than a primary designated offence, that is
@ref s 487.04 "secondary designated offence" (the lead-in: other than a primary designated offence) (src:9425)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 487.04 facts of the offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.04 the offence is a secondary designated offence` MEANS
    IF `s 487.04 the offence is a primary designated offence` facts EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "secondary designated offence means an offence, other than a primary designated offence, that is"
    ELSE CONSIDER facts's `how the person is charged`
         WHEN `s 487.04 with the listed offence itself` THEN `s 487.04 the paragraphs of a definition are read together` (`s 487.04 secondary designated offence the answer of each of paragraphs (a) to (d.2)` facts TRUE)
         WHEN `s 487.04 with an attempt to commit the listed offence` THEN `s 487.04 secondary designated offence (e) an attempt or a conspiracy` facts
         WHEN `s 487.04 with a conspiracy to commit the listed offence` THEN `s 487.04 secondary designated offence (e) an attempt or a conspiracy` facts

§ `Section 487.04 -- designated offence`

-- designated offence means a primary designated offence or a secondary designated offence.
-- src:9294 | designated offence means a primary designated offence or a secondary designated offence; (infraction désignée)
@ref s 487.04 "designated offence" (src:9294)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 487.04 facts of the offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.04 the offence is a designated offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 487.04 the offence is a primary designated offence` facts EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`s 487.04 the offence is a secondary designated offence` facts EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`s 487.04 the offence is a primary designated offence` facts EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`s 487.04 the offence is a secondary designated offence` facts EQUALS NOTHING) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): one limb turns on a maximum punishment the offence's own section does not state
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "designated offence means a primary designated offence or a secondary designated offence"
